\f0\b0 \cf0 For an ATAK client to be able to connect to the server using the servers authority the device must have the truststore-intermediate-ca.p12 file.\
\
The easiest way to get the client onto the server is to create a DataPackage (a zipped file) with the trust store-intermediate-ca.p12 file, a manifest and a preference file with the server IP address.\
\
When you downloaded the MASTER_SERVER_NAME_FOLDER_STRUCTURE it came with a boiler plate profile preference file and a manifest you can modify to reflect this information.\
\
Once the datapackage is created you can share that out with the user\'92s unique username and password you created using the TAK-Server GUI.\
\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 [Install LetsEncrypt Keys - Not Required] This will allow you to use the enroll for certificate from ATAK using a public facing domain.\
\
Step 1 - go to your domain host provider like go daddy.com and add an A record to point to the IP address of the TAK-Server\
\
After the A record had been changed now log into terminal or the web console of your virtual machine.\
\
This script will also add what is called a cronjob to your server which will mostly automatically renew your LetsEncrypt certificate.\
\
